// pdlvds_h723.repl — STM32H723 platform for the LVDS receiver, Renode format.
// UNTESTED: authored from the design sources, never executed (REFUSAL-RECORD.md).
//
// RECONCILED 2026-11-10 (first execution attempt): the standalone
// MappedMemory block that used to follow is REPLACED by an include of
// Renode's bundled STM32H743 CPU platform. Verified before the swap:
// the bundled stm32h7.repl map is IDENTICAL to the linker.ld map below
// (flashBank1 1 MB @ 0x08000000, dtcm 128 KB @ 0x20000000, axiSram
// 512 KB @ 0x24000000) and it brings the Cortex-M7 cpu + the H7
// peripheral models (RCC/PWR/GPIO/OTG_HS/SPI/I2C) this file only
// listed. The H743 model stands in for the H723 (near-identical
// peripheral sets for the blocks below, per the original note).
//
// HOW TO USE: start from Renode's bundled STM32H7 platform file
//   (find renode -iname '*stm32h7*' -name '*.repl')
// and reconcile it against this file: the memory map below is authoritative
// for THIS design (from firmware/linker.ld); the peripheral list is the set
// the firmware actually touches (firmware/src/board.h, hw/CONNECTIONS.md).
// Addresses follow the repo's own convention: VERIFY against RM0468.
//
// Memory map (firmware/linker.ld):
//   FLASH    0x08000000  1024K
//   DTCM     0x20000000   128K   (stack lives here: _estack = top of DTCM)
//   AXI SRAM 0x24000000   512K
//
// cpu: STM32H723 is a Cortex-M7 (use Renode's bundled H7 CPU/peripheral
// models where they exist; the H723 and H743 peripheral sets are near
// identical for the blocks below).
//
// Peripherals the firmware drives (board.h bases, all VERIFY vs RM0468):
//   RCC        0x58024400   clocks.c — must at least accept the PLL config
//   PWR        0x58024800   USB33DEN bit is written by the USB glue
//   SYSCFG     0x58000400   PMCR analog switches (ULPI PC2_C/PC3_C)
//   GPIOA..H   0x58020000+  ULPI on AF10, USB3300 reset on PA4 (active high)
//   OTG_HS     USB device controller, ULPI external PHY (USB3300);
//              firmware runs the DWC2 in slave (non-DMA) mode
//   SPI3                  DAC8562, SYNC = PA15 (per schematic; see
//                         hw/CONNECTIONS.md) — threshold path
//   I2C1/I2C2  0x40005400 / 0x40005800   TMP117 + config devices
//   ADN2813 CDR           modelled boundary: recovered clock/data enter
//                         the capture path; CDR lock behaviour is a
//                         stimulus parameter, not an emulated chip
//   Capture input         comparator's digitized chip stream arrives via
//                         the timer/SPI-slave capture the firmware arms
//                         in capture.c — inject the codec chain's chip
//                         stream here (Manchester 16 Mbaud, PRBS-15)

using "platforms/cpus/stm32h743.repl"
